"tab_1":{
"title":" What Is a Mutual Fund Screener?",
"description":"<p>A mutual fund screener is a tool that helps investors shortlist mutual funds by applying filters such as category, returns, risk level, expense ratio, fund size, and fund age. Instead of manually reviewing hundreds of schemes, you define your criteria once, and the screener shows only those funds that match. In practical terms, it works like search filters for mutual funds. You decide what matters, and the tool does the sorting.</p>
<p>Mutual fund screeners are available on most investment platforms and financial websites and exist primarily to solve one problem: choice overload. Indian investors have access to well over a thousand mutual fund schemes across equity, debt, hybrid, and solution-oriented categories. Evaluating each option manually is not realistic when every fund comes with multiple data points, such as returns across time periods, portfolio holdings, risk measures, and costs. A screener brings all this information together and narrows the universe to a manageable shortlist.</p>
",
